messages:
oliver: Putting this here — found a webpack/rollup/vite edge bundling quirk that reproduces an auth-on-retry failure. Repro included, small and deterministic.

sana: can you summarise the failure in one line?

oliver: sure: when packaging the JS SDK as ESM for edge runtimes some bundlers emit an interop helper that reconstructs Request objects using `new Request(req, ...)` which in our edge shim loses the Authorization header on retry. CJS builds retain `req.clone()` and work.

marco: ah, similar to other reports but did you find what triggers the helper change? webpack/terser? ts types?

oliver: this one was specifically tied to two things we didn't expect together: 1) using `exports` conditional fields to point at ESM + CJS entries, and 2) a TypeScript-generated helper that annotated Request as a plain object in d.ts which let terser think clone() wasn't required and tree-shake the polyfill. When the polyfill disappears, some bundlers fallback to building a Request from the plain object.

abby: can you paste the repro steps (exact commands)?

oliver: yep — minimal repro in the repo: https://example/repro-edge-webpack. Steps:
1) git clone https://example/repro-edge-webpack && cd repro-edge-webpack
2) npm ci
3) npm run build:edge:webpack   # builds dist/esm using webpack target that picks exports.import
4) npm run serve:edge          # local edge runtime shim (mimics cloud edge fetch semantics)
5) curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer SECRET" http://localhost:8787/api/proxy

Observed: first proxied request 200, then SDK retry happens and retry returns 403. Inspecting logs shows Authorization header present for original request, missing for the retry.

marco: what does the built helper look like?

oliver: snippet from dist/esm/edge-helper.js:
```js
function retry(req){
  // injected by bundler interop transform
  const reconstructed = new Request(req.url, req);
  return fetch(reconstructed);
}
```

oliver: contrast with dist/cjs/index.js:
```js
function retry(req){
  const r = req.clone();
  return fetch(r);
}
```

sana: interesting. Did you try import style (default vs namespace) or changing exports config?

oliver: yes — `import * as SDK from 'redwood-sdk'` in some cases forced Rollup to take a different interop path and avoided the helper, but that's not reliable across plugin sets or webpack versions. Changing package exports to point to CJS for consumers helped but breaks ESM-only users, so not a good general fix.

abby: proposed fix?

oliver: short-term SDK change: defensive cloning helper that prefers `req.clone()` and falls back to reconstructing a Request while explicitly copying headers as an iterable (preserves Authorization). Example we validated in the repro: 
```js
function safeCloneRequest(req){
  if (typeof req.clone === 'function') return req.clone();
  const headers = new Headers();
  for (const [k,v] of (req.headers || [])) headers.set(k,v);
  return new Request(req.url, { method: req.method, headers, body: req.body });
}
```

oliver: added that to the SDK in the repro branch and the bundle matrix (webpack, rollup, vite) keeps Authorization on retries in our local edge shim.

marco: good, but watch out for streaming bodies — reconstructing a Request can consume the body or lose streaming semantics. Did you test POST streaming?

oliver: yes — currently validated only buffered JSON bodies (typical use). We explicitly called out streaming and keepalive in the PR & tests and asked eng-runtime to review for platform-specific semantics.

sana: created GH issue redwood/sdk#5120 and assigned eng-runtime + bundler-experts. Please link repro and the CI matrix.

triage-bot: Issue created: redwood/sdk#5120 1 assigned to @marco and @eng-runtime. CI matrix queued (webpack, rollup, vite).

abby: small doc mitigation: add a note under SDK "Edge bundler quirks" recommending namespace import as a temporary workaround and linking the repro. Also add a test in our SDK CI that builds an edge ESM bundle with at least one bundler.

oliver: pushed branch devex/webpack-edge-clone-fallback with the safeClone change, unit tests, and a cross-bundler CI job. Link: https://example/repro-edge-webpack/compare/devex/webpack-edge-clone-fallback

marco: i'll review the PR for streaming and semantic compatibility with native edge fetch. If OK we'll merge and cut a minor release and update the docs.

sana: thanks team 44D — good catch before a customer hit this in prod."
